WEBVTT

00:02:31.518 --> 00:02:35.955
Omen

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.957
A date, you say!?

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:43.721
Yeah. She's one of the seniors
from high school...

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:45.424
Hold on a second, Saya.

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:48.957
Have you already forgotten
about the mixer we just had?

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.867
Of course I remember!

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:55.736
Oh, big brother,
you've got to be more positive.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:03:00.075
At this rate, things won't go well,
even if the girl likes you!

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:01.774
Here's your lunch.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:04.078
That's not the point!

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:07.678
She's really beautiful, too.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.383
And she says that
she's never had a boyfriend.

00:03:11.424 --> 00:03:13.187
Don't you think that's a shame?

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.626
Are you even listening
to what I'm saying?

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:18.028
Uh-huh.
I'm definitely listening.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:20.464
Thanks to you, that mixer...

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:24.334
Oh! Big brother, you're leaving
the salad again!

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.395
That's no good.
You've got to be sure to eat it!

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.135
I-I hate tomatoes!

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.735
If you don't eat your vegetables,
you won't grow up to be big!

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:34.804
Shut up!
I'm going out!

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:37.839
She works for the crime lab,
by the way.

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:39.715
Hmm? The crime lab?

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:42.880
You mean the place
where they examine corpses...

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.514
...stray hairs,
and other strange things?

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.319
Yeah.

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:49.226
And that's why she understands
what we do for a living.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:52.026
In that case, it's even more reason
to say no to a disgusting woman...

00:03:52.065 --> 00:03:55.557
...who would shut herself away
for a year.

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:57.433
Okay, I'm going ahead!

00:03:57.470 --> 00:04:00.530
Oh, big brother, your lunch!

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:06.740
Geez...

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:09.907
Not matter how much we do,
it just doesn't go away.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:12.975
This isn't much different from when
we were working at a police box.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:16.011
That might have been preferable.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.717
I mean, there weren't any
shaved eyebrow...

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.953
...pomade-using bastards
at the police box, you know?

00:04:20.994 --> 00:04:23.258
You dummy,
what if he overheard you?

00:04:24.364 --> 00:04:26.195
Did you find it?

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:28.097
No, not yet.

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.126
It's the same here.

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.069
Huh?

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.507
All of the case files have been pulled.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:40.171
It looks like we've got no choice
but to go to the crime lab.

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:42.113
The crime lab, sir?

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:45.481
Yeah, it looks like every bit
of data and evidence

00:04:45.518 --> 00:04:48.646
we've gathered on the monsters
is collected there.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:49.347
What?

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.947
In that case, shouldn't we head there
right away?

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.481
That's impossible.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:55.255
Chief?

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:57.525
Now, this is just a rumor...

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:59.758
...but the crime lab is under
the jurisdiction of the Security Section.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:01.426
We can't just carelessly take
any actions.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.401
That's why we need proof!

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:06.633
Proof that we can use to make
mincemeat out of them!

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:16.473
What? Really?
You want to meet her now?

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:18.279
What happened, big brother?

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:20.650
Never mind that, just hurry up
and set things up.

00:05:20.687 --> 00:05:22.746
You don't have to push yourself.

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:25.349
Senior Yukino is pretty busy, too,
you know.

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:28.360
Hey, you're the one
who brought this up!

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.726
I wonder what should I do?

00:05:45.211 --> 00:05:46.200
- Hmm?
- Hmm?

00:05:54.554 --> 00:05:56.647
Oh, man.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:59.920
I should have asked for a picture
or something before I came here.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:07.830
Well, she IS a scientist, so she's
probably nothing to write home about.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.228
Mr. Shindo?

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:11.930
Huh? Oh!

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:18.343
You're Ranmaru, right?
I'm Yukino Shiraishi.

00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:21.836
Oh...

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:24.782
N-Nice to meet you.

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:27.945
You really do look like Saya.

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:30.478
R-Really?

00:06:30.523 --> 00:06:32.684
I'm not sure if I should be happy or not.

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.419
U-Umm...

00:06:37.463 --> 00:06:38.191
Yes?

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:41.223
What did Saya say about today?

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:44.464
"Take your time
and enjoy the whole day."

00:06:44.504 --> 00:06:49.737
Oh, but those are
her words verbatim.

00:06:49.776 --> 00:06:51.767
R-Right.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:57.342
I'm sorry.
I'm not really used to this.

00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:01.251
Actually, this is pretty much
the first time for me, too.

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:04.621
No way.

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:06.249
It's true.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:10.422
I've been busy taking care
of my little sister since the incident.

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:11.623
No, reverse that.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:14.758
She's had her hands full
taking care of me, maybe?

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:16.268
No, wait, that's not it.

00:07:17.136 --> 00:07:18.626
You two are really close, aren't you?

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:19.638
Huh?

00:07:19.672 --> 00:07:23.108
Saya was always talking
about you, Ranmaru.

00:07:23.142 --> 00:07:24.302
W-What about?

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:27.107
Huh? What about?
Well, a lot of things.

00:07:27.146 --> 00:07:28.511
A lot of things!?

00:07:28.548 --> 00:07:29.879
Yes.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:38.589
Famous Shibuya Soba

00:07:43.696 --> 00:07:45.561
Oh, big brother!

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:49.762
You're on a date, and you take
Senior Yukino to a place like that?

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:52.737
Hanazono, could you get the car
a little closer?

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:55.172
I-I can, but...

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:03.080
This is tasty.

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:06.084
That really looks delicious,
doesn't it?

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:09.053
Oh, what kind of stupidity
is he pulling now?

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:10.749
He's so embarrassing!

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.087
H-Hey...

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.284
What?

00:08:13.326 --> 00:08:16.762
How about we, you know,
get some food, too?

00:08:16.796 --> 00:08:17.990
Huh?

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:23.158
Sorry to keep you waiting!
This will warm you up!

00:08:23.202 --> 00:08:25.500
Thank you.

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:28.334
It's delicious!

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:29.841
I heard this from Saya...

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:30.535
Huh?

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:33.739
You work in the crime lab,
right, Miss Shiraishi?

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.542
You can call me Yukino.

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:37.071
O-Okay.

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:40.677
It seems that society mistakenly thinks
women like me are gloomy...

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.883
...because we work in places like that.

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:45.686
T-That's not true.

00:08:45.725 --> 00:08:48.455
There are a lot of times
when we start our research...

00:08:48.494 --> 00:08:50.394
...where we get caught up in it...

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:55.128
...and spend several days straight
working, forgetting to even eat.

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:58.261
But that's how I feel normally.

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:01.637
Our world really is strange, isn't it?

00:09:01.674 --> 00:09:06.077
Miss Shiraishi...
I mean, Yukino, what do you do?

00:09:06.112 --> 00:09:10.742
I-I mean, they say that the crime lab
examines corpses and stuff.

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:13.513
It's called the Forensics Laboratory...

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:16.989
...and they test the blood,
bodily fluids, hair and tissue...

00:09:17.023 --> 00:09:19.651
...that are left behind
at crime scenes.

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:23.184
I'm part of the documents laboratory...

00:09:23.229 --> 00:09:26.494
...so I mostly do boring work
like handwriting analysis...

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.762
...and impression analysis.

00:09:28.801 --> 00:09:31.031
What other groups are there?

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:34.699
The chemistry laboratory,
which tests drugs.

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:39.541
There's also the psychology laboratory,
which uses polygraph tests, and...

00:09:39.579 --> 00:09:41.206
Hmm?

00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:41.941
No...

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:42.777
Hmm?

00:09:42.815 --> 00:09:45.181
It's nothing.

00:09:48.321 --> 00:09:49.413
Ranmaru?

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:51.980
Actually, I have a favor to ask.

00:09:52.024 --> 00:09:53.958
Oh?

00:09:55.261 --> 00:09:58.253
Thanks for everything today,
Hanazono.

00:09:58.297 --> 00:10:03.030
You drove the patrol car for me,
and you even treated me to lunch!

00:10:03.069 --> 00:10:05.162
Okay, then, see you next time!

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:09.538
What? Um, Saya?

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:17.272
Now then, now I need to check how
things went after that.

00:10:20.653 --> 00:10:25.147
The number you have called is currently
either out of range or turned off.

00:10:25.191 --> 00:10:27.056
What?

00:10:36.402 --> 00:10:37.869
Out of Service Area
Well...

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:40.167
...we're off-duty today,
so there's no need to call them.

00:10:42.775 --> 00:10:44.299
I'm sorry.

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:46.811
Security has gotten
pretty strict recently.

00:10:46.846 --> 00:10:48.905
I'm sorry,
asking you for the impossible.

00:10:48.948 --> 00:10:51.075
But why did you want to come here?

00:10:51.117 --> 00:10:55.110
I kind of thought that I'd like to see
where you worked, Yukino.

00:10:55.154 --> 00:10:58.851
Oh? R-Really?

00:11:10.369 --> 00:11:11.734
Ranmaru?

00:11:11.771 --> 00:11:12.760
What's this place?

00:11:12.805 --> 00:11:16.536
That is where they do research
on bacteria and viruses and such.

00:11:16.575 --> 00:11:20.511
That's why we're not allowed
to come and go as we please.

00:11:28.754 --> 00:11:31.120
This is where I work.

00:11:31.157 --> 00:11:32.317
I see.

00:11:32.358 --> 00:11:34.383
I'll make us some coffee or something.

00:11:34.427 --> 00:11:35.894
Oh, thanks.

00:11:42.234 --> 00:11:43.394
Is something the matter?

00:11:43.436 --> 00:11:46.098
N-No, nothing.

00:11:46.138 --> 00:11:48.129
You like your coffee black, right?

00:11:48.174 --> 00:11:48.936
Huh?

00:11:48.974 --> 00:11:50.737
Saya told me.

00:11:50.776 --> 00:11:52.676
R-Really?

00:11:52.712 --> 00:11:55.306
She also said that you hate
tomatoes and celery.

00:11:55.347 --> 00:11:57.474
She even told you that?

00:11:58.017 --> 00:12:00.110
T-That's not it.

00:12:00.152 --> 00:12:03.087
She always makes
the things I dislike on purpose, so...

00:12:03.122 --> 00:12:06.922
Then maybe I should come by
and make you dinner sometime.

00:12:06.959 --> 00:12:08.017
What?

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:13.123
I may lock myself away in my lab,
but I'm good at cooking.

00:12:13.165 --> 00:12:15.030
Well, that is...

00:12:15.067 --> 00:12:18.036
Oh, but I wonder
if Saya would be against it.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.630
Don't worry about her any more.

00:12:20.673 --> 00:12:23.369
By the way, what are
you researching, Yukino?

00:12:27.947 --> 00:12:30.711
We don't just analyze documents here.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.412
We also do archaeology
research as well.

00:12:33.452 --> 00:12:35.010
Archaeology?

00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:38.148
We get requests from the government
and related organizations...

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.420
...to analyze buried cultural properties.

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:44.418
That's why I've been shut up in here
so much recently.

00:12:44.463 --> 00:12:45.930
Hmm?

00:12:47.133 --> 00:12:48.259
This book is...

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:52.361
This is something that was found
in an old church in southern Italy.

00:12:52.404 --> 00:12:54.998
So you're researching old books
like this one.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.942
Yes, and there is something extremely
interesting written in this one.

00:12:58.978 --> 00:13:01.640
You've heard the term
'alchemist', right?

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.672
Yeah, you mean the ones
that can change lead into gold?

00:13:04.717 --> 00:13:08.278
Looking at it scientifically,
it's impossible...

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:12.450
...but they wrote that every substance
in the world contains a spirit.

00:13:12.491 --> 00:13:17.155
And they believed that if you could
call forth those spirits...

00:13:17.196 --> 00:13:19.994
...and rearrange the elements...

00:13:20.032 --> 00:13:23.934
...then you could turn lead into gold
or even create life.

00:13:23.969 --> 00:13:26.665
This is the alchemists at the time.

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:30.664
And this is the spirit
that they called forth.

00:13:33.779 --> 00:13:36.270
What's written right here?

00:13:36.315 --> 00:13:39.182
It's Latin, and it says,
'The Secrets of Druj'.

00:13:39.218 --> 00:13:40.242
Druj?

00:13:40.286 --> 00:13:43.187
It's originally the name of a devil
that is mentioned in Persian myth,

00:13:43.222 --> 00:13:46.749
and it means "immoral" or "deceit".

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.750
A devil.

00:13:59.071 --> 00:14:01.733
In other words, they believed that if you
could use the powers of these spirits...

00:14:01.774 --> 00:14:04.641
...you could become immortal.

00:14:04.677 --> 00:14:08.408
And thus, the aristocracy of the time,
in order to obtain eternal power,

00:14:08.447 --> 00:14:11.939
ordered the alchemists
to bring forth these spirits.

00:14:11.984 --> 00:14:17.752
Of course, I don't believe
in spirits and such.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.850
Who in the world
is making you research this?

00:14:20.893 --> 00:14:23.794
It looks like it's an organization
related to the government...

00:14:23.829 --> 00:14:25.854
...but I really don't know.

00:14:25.898 --> 00:14:29.834
That kind of stuff is handled
by the people higher up, after all.

00:14:35.441 --> 00:14:36.430
This is...

00:14:36.475 --> 00:14:37.635
What's the matter?

00:14:37.676 --> 00:14:41.168
I've seen something like this before!

00:14:41.213 --> 00:14:42.202
What?

00:14:42.248 --> 00:14:44.375
No, there's no mistaking it.

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:47.146
This face!
This face is from that time...

00:14:48.454 --> 00:14:49.443
Father.

00:14:49.488 --> 00:14:51.581
What? "Father"?

00:14:51.624 --> 00:14:53.091
This is my father.

00:14:53.125 --> 00:14:57.425
This place is off-limits to outsiders.

00:14:57.463 --> 00:15:01.695
Oh... I'm sorry for making her show
this to me, but...

00:15:01.734 --> 00:15:05.636
If you don't have any other business
here, then please leave!

00:15:05.671 --> 00:15:09.937
Father, you don't have to say it like that!
After he came all this way!

00:15:09.975 --> 00:15:13.035
Yukino, have you forgotten the rules?

00:15:13.078 --> 00:15:15.603
But he's a detective from the Shibuya
Special Mobile Investigation Force!

00:15:15.648 --> 00:15:17.013
Detective?

00:15:17.049 --> 00:15:19.517
I'm sorry I didn't mention this sooner.
My name is Shindo.

00:15:19.551 --> 00:15:22.213
Actually, there was something
I wanted to look into.

00:15:25.291 --> 00:15:26.280
Leave!

00:15:36.468 --> 00:15:37.457
I'm sorry.

00:15:38.504 --> 00:15:41.371
He didn't used to be like that.

00:15:41.407 --> 00:15:43.637
Is your father in the same section?

00:15:43.676 --> 00:15:47.840
No, my father is the director
of the special biology laboratory.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.472
Special biology?

00:15:49.515 --> 00:15:52.177
It's beyond the doorway
with the metal grill.

00:15:54.019 --> 00:15:55.486
Okay then, Ranmaru.

00:15:55.521 --> 00:15:57.512
I'm going to head back
to the laboratory.

00:15:57.556 --> 00:15:59.490
What?
Wasn't today a day off for you?

00:15:59.525 --> 00:16:01.891
Yes, but actually I still have work
that I need to do.

00:16:01.927 --> 00:16:03.019
I see.

00:16:03.062 --> 00:16:03.960
See you.

00:16:03.996 --> 00:16:05.486
Umm, Yukino.

00:16:05.531 --> 00:16:06.190
Yes?

00:16:06.231 --> 00:16:09.359
About what I said earlier, about
something I wanted to look into...

00:16:09.401 --> 00:16:10.299
Oh.

00:16:10.336 --> 00:16:13.362
You know about the scattered body part
murder case, right?

00:16:13.405 --> 00:16:14.201
Yes.

00:16:14.239 --> 00:16:16.605
Including the fact that the culprit
is not a human?

00:16:16.642 --> 00:16:18.974
Oh!

00:16:19.011 --> 00:16:21.741
I've seen it.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.839
And it looks just like the monster...

00:16:23.882 --> 00:16:26.180
...that's in the book
that you're researching, Yukino.

00:16:27.619 --> 00:16:29.678
It was a seriously monstrous thing.

00:16:29.722 --> 00:16:33.123
But for some unknown reason, all of
the evidence on it has disappeared.

00:16:35.094 --> 00:16:37.995
And there's talk that the evidence...

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:40.965
...has been brought to somewhere
in this laboratory.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.968
Ranmaru.

00:16:43.002 --> 00:16:46.597
Well, it's true that there are various
rumors around here.

00:16:48.007 --> 00:16:49.338
But...

00:16:52.044 --> 00:16:55.172
I'm sorry, I have to go now!

00:16:55.214 --> 00:16:58.149
Wait, Yukino!

00:17:06.892 --> 00:17:08.757
What's this?

00:17:08.794 --> 00:17:10.785
Please take a look.

00:17:10.829 --> 00:17:11.818
Hmm?

00:17:13.399 --> 00:17:15.196
Don't they look similar?

00:17:15.234 --> 00:17:16.223
Hmm.

00:17:16.268 --> 00:17:18.600
What in the world is this?

00:17:18.637 --> 00:17:20.264
I'll show you the whole thing.

00:17:22.041 --> 00:17:26.501
This was taken from a fresco
drawn in the Vatican

00:17:26.545 --> 00:17:28.274
at the beginning
of the 13th century.

00:17:28.313 --> 00:17:31.646
What in the world
is this disgusting thing?

00:17:31.683 --> 00:17:36.484
A demon... or it might possibly
be called a devil.

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:49.392
What is that, hold on a second!

00:17:50.869 --> 00:17:52.734
What's up with you?

00:17:52.771 --> 00:17:54.398
Big brother?

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:56.203
Ohh, big brother!

00:17:56.241 --> 00:17:58.801
Huh? Oh, it's you.

00:17:58.844 --> 00:18:00.402
So, how did it go?

00:18:00.446 --> 00:18:01.435
Did what go?

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:03.345
The date with Senior Yukino!

00:18:03.382 --> 00:18:06.545
Oh, that... not bad, I guess.

00:18:06.585 --> 00:18:07.847
What's with that?

00:18:07.886 --> 00:18:10.320
You came back all down in the dumps...

00:18:10.355 --> 00:18:14.382
...so I've been tiptoeing around you
since I figured she dumped you.

00:18:14.426 --> 00:18:17.224
Dummy, don't think so little of me!

00:18:17.262 --> 00:18:19.730
Okay.

00:18:19.765 --> 00:18:24.099
Hey, has Yukino's old man always
been like that?

00:18:24.136 --> 00:18:25.228
Like what?

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:29.206
Grouchy, I guess,
or maybe unapproachable.

00:18:29.241 --> 00:18:30.868
Who knows?

00:18:30.909 --> 00:18:32.774
It's just that there was
that incident before.

00:18:32.811 --> 00:18:33.539
Incident?

00:18:33.579 --> 00:18:37.811
Yeah, Senior Yukino's mother
was killed during a robbery.

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:41.479
A robbery?
Did they catch the culprit?

00:18:41.520 --> 00:18:42.782
Hmm...

00:18:42.821 --> 00:18:45.289
Well, the police worked
really hard to find him...

00:18:45.324 --> 00:18:47.792
...but even the mass media
eventually wrote...

00:18:47.826 --> 00:18:49.487
...that it might be an unsolvable case.

00:18:49.528 --> 00:18:52.793
Hey, Saya,
when did that incident happen?

00:18:52.831 --> 00:18:57.962
What? Umm, she said it was two years
before I started high school.

00:18:58.003 --> 00:18:59.402
Five years ago!?

00:18:59.438 --> 00:19:01.531
I guess it's around that long ago.

00:19:02.908 --> 00:19:04.273
What's the matter?

00:19:06.044 --> 00:19:08.911
Saya, what's Yukino's home number?

00:19:08.947 --> 00:19:12.439
What? She didn't tell you?
Oh, you're hopeless.

00:19:12.484 --> 00:19:14.315
Never mind that,
hurry up and tell me!

00:19:14.353 --> 00:19:16.617
Huh? What day is it today?

00:19:16.655 --> 00:19:18.520
What day it is doesn't matter, does it?

00:19:18.557 --> 00:19:20.923
It does.
Depending on what day it is...

00:19:20.959 --> 00:19:23.757
...Senior Yukino will be staying
at the lab on night duty.

00:19:38.977 --> 00:19:41.878
Hey, did you hear something?

00:19:41.914 --> 00:19:44.144
It's probably just your imagination.

00:19:48.720 --> 00:19:49.379
Hey!

00:19:49.421 --> 00:19:50.649
It's coming from over there!

00:19:58.197 --> 00:19:59.960
W-What are you doing?

00:20:03.402 --> 00:20:08.066
We're very sorry,
but today's services have ended.

00:20:10.943 --> 00:20:15.141
The number you have called
is currently either out of range...

00:20:15.180 --> 00:20:15.839
Damn!

00:20:15.881 --> 00:20:19.214
If I had known this,
I wouldn't have left Yukino alone.

00:20:26.225 --> 00:20:27.419
Hey, open up!

00:20:41.974 --> 00:20:43.908
Look at what it's done.

00:20:50.349 --> 00:20:53.216
So you've finally shown yourself.

00:20:53.252 --> 00:20:57.882
You've been able to rampage
to your heart's content... up until now.

00:20:59.091 --> 00:21:00.456
There's no way I can forgive you!

00:21:04.196 --> 00:21:06.323
Damn it, so it's really no use.

00:21:32.224 --> 00:21:35.387
D-Damn it...

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:56.340
It can't be.

00:22:09.528 --> 00:22:11.120
Damn, it got away.

00:22:12.664 --> 00:22:13.858
Shindo!

00:22:14.966 --> 00:22:16.194
Rokujo.

00:22:16.234 --> 00:22:17.792
Are you all right?

00:22:17.836 --> 00:22:18.894
Yeah, somehow.

00:22:20.806 --> 00:22:25.505
That's a surprise... being able to survive
an attack from Number Twelve.

00:22:25.544 --> 00:22:27.068
Just as I thought.

00:22:27.112 --> 00:22:28.443
So he really is...

00:22:29.348 --> 00:22:30.940
They're mingling.

00:22:41.593 --> 00:22:46.360
Sono te wo tsunaidari

00:22:46.398 --> 00:22:51.335
Kuchizuke attari

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:56.137
Ato sukoshi de sotto

